#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:225
msgid "Create a 1-D CUDA kernel launch and unpack the single block index:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:227
msgid ""
"with T.Kernel(T.ceildiv(N, 128), threads=128) as bx:\n"
"    # bx is the blockIdx.x binding (also iterable as (bx,))\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:233
msgid "Launch a 2-D grid while requesting two thread dimensions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:235
msgid ""
"with T.Kernel(grid_x, grid_y, threads=(64, 2)) as (bx, by):\n"
"    tx, ty = T.get_thread_bindings()\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:244
msgid ""
"Construct a kernel launch frame with a CUDA thread block cluster (SM90+ "
"only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:247
msgid ""
"This is the CUDA-specific variant of :func:`Kernel`: identical launch "
"semantics and bindings, plus a ``cluster_dims`` annotation. The kernel will "
"be launched with cudaLaunchKernelEx using "
"cudaLaunchAttributeClusterDimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:254
msgid ""
"The cluster dimensions. For example, use 2 or (2, 1, 1) to create 2-CTA "
"clusters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:257
msgid ""
"A integer representing blockDim.x Or a list of integers representing "
"blockDim.(x|y|z)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:266
msgid ""
"with T.ClusterKernel(grid_x, grid_y, cluster_dims=2, threads=128) as (bx, "
"by):\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:276
msgid ""
"The code must follows the following rules: 1. The kernel source must be a "
"valid CUDA kernel which can be correctly compiled under TileLang's context. "
"2. The kernel source must either contains only one `__global__` function as "
"an entry, or have a `__global__` entry function named `main_kernel`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:280
msgid ""
"Inline CUDA source code, or a path to a CUDA source file. If the argument "
"resolves to an existing file, the file contents are loaded. Otherwise it is "
"treated as inline CUDA source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:286
msgid ""
"Optional name of the `__global__` CUDA entry function inside the provided "
"source. When specified, TileLang launches that external CUDA entry directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/kernel/index.rst:294
msgid ""
"The cluster dimensions for SM90+ cluster launch. For example, use 2 or (2, "
"1, 1) to create 2-CTA clusters. When specified, the kernel will be launched "
"using cudaLaunchKernelEx with cudaLaunchAttributeClusterDimension."
msgstr ""
